WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.887
Apollo Q Labs. Level one, module one: what an option is.

2
00:00:06.187 --> 00:00:09.793
An option is a contract on one hundred shares of a stock.

3
00:00:09.793 --> 00:00:16.365
It has a strike price (the fixed price you can buy or sell at) and an expiration date (the option’s last day).

4
00:00:16.665 --> 00:00:22.427
A call gives the buyer the right, but not the obligation, to buy the shares at the strike.

5
00:00:22.427 --> 00:00:26.183
A put gives the buyer the right to sell the shares at the strike.

6
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:29.556
For every buyer, there is a seller, called the writer.

7
00:00:29.556 --> 00:00:39.648
The writer is paid the premium (the price of the option) and takes on the obligation to buy or sell the shares if the buyer exercises (chooses to use the option).

8
00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:44.813
Prices are quoted per share, but one contract covers one hundred shares.

9
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:51.428
So, a call priced at two dollars and fifty cents costs two hundred and fifty dollars per contract.

10
00:00:51.428 --> 00:00:53.904
Two contracts cost five hundred.

11
00:00:54.204 --> 00:00:59.965
A long call at expiration: buy the one oh five call for two dollars, or two hundred dollars.

12
00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:04.660
At or below one oh five, the loss is the two hundred dollars paid, and no more.

13
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:12.512
Break even is one oh seven (the stock price where you neither gain nor lose). At one fifteen, the gain is eight hundred dollars.

14
00:01:12.812 --> 00:01:20.237
A long put is the opposite. Buy the ninety five put for one dollar eighty, or one hundred and eighty dollars.

15
00:01:20.237 --> 00:01:26.425
Break even is ninety three twenty. At eighty five, the gain is eight hundred and twenty dollars.

16
00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:30.011
At or above ninety five, the full premium is lost.

17
00:01:30.311 --> 00:01:37.480
U.S. stock options are American style: the holder can exercise on any business day until expiration.

18
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:45.567
At expiration, options in the money by one cent or more are exercised automatically, unless the holder instructs otherwise.

19
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:51.264
Most traders close before expiration, by trading the option back, rather than exercising.

20
00:01:51.564 --> 00:01:58.755
Recap: a call is the right to buy, a put is the right to sell, and one contract covers one hundred shares.

21
00:01:58.755 --> 00:02:02.617
Next, read the lessons, then take the six question quiz.

